# Question: when a daemon is killed while a container runs, does the next
# daemon remove the container it left before it starts anything, and then run
# the configured container exactly once, as a new process, with a warning that
# names it (spec-container-1-runtime AC-12, the container-leftover-swept test)?
#
# A unit test cannot decide it: a killed daemon leaves a real process in a
# real control group, a mounted overlay and the runtime library's state
# directory, which refuses a new container of the same name. Only a real
# kernel shows whether the sweep kills, unmounts and removes them, and whether
# the library then creates the container again.
#
# Method: the first daemon starts the container, whose probe appends a line
# to /starts in its writable layer at each start. The daemon is killed with
# SIGKILL, so no drain runs and the container keeps running: it took a session
# of its own. A second daemon starts on the same config. The probe's starts
# mode waits for the second line, then requires exactly two starts and exactly
# one process in the container's control group: a sweep that did not kill the
# leftover leaves two processes there, or no second start at all, because the
# library refuses a name whose state directory is still in place.
#
# The store lives under /run, not in the test's work directory: in the QEMU
# guest that directory is on the 9p share of the checkout, and an overlay
# cannot take a 9p directory as its upper layer.
option=needs-linux:caps=sys-admin
option=exclusive:group=container
option=timeout:value=120s
option=env:var=ze.test.container.store:value=/run/ze-container-test-$PORT

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONFIG
container {
	instance probe {
		image probe
	}
}
EOF_CONFIG

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-containerprobe reset /run/ze-container-test-$PORT:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=config:name=first
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze-containerprobe verify /run/ze-container-test-$PORT probe:timeout=45s:exit=0
cmd=stop:seq=4:name=first:signal=kill
cmd=background:seq=5:exec=ze -:stdin=config:name=second
cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze-containerprobe starts /run/ze-container-test-$PORT probe 2:timeout=50s:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=probe: the container started 2 times
expect=stdout:contains=probe: one process runs in its control group
expect=stderr:contains=a previous run left this container running
reject=stdout:contains=probe: FAIL
